    <item>
      <title>Firebase Data Denormalization: Syncing Usernames Across Messages</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/javascript/firebase-denormalization-sync-usernames/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/javascript/firebase-denormalization-sync-usernames/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;firebase-data-denormalization-syncing-usernames-across-messages&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;Firebase Data Denormalization: Syncing Usernames Across Messages&amp;rdquo;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Consider a scenario with a chat application where we store &lt;code&gt;users&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;messages&lt;/code&gt;. To display message author names efficiently, we duplicate the &lt;code&gt;username&lt;/code&gt; within each &lt;code&gt;message&lt;/code&gt; entry, alongside a reference to the &lt;code&gt;user&lt;/code&gt;&amp;rsquo;s primary profile.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s a simplified data structure:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-json&#34; data-lang=&#34;json&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;users&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;so:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;209103&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;name:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Frank van Puffelen&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;location:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;San Francisco, CA&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;questionCount:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;so:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;3648524&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;name:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;legolandbridge&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;location:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;London, Prague, Barcelona&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;questionCount:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;-Jabhsay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;3487&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;message:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;How to write denormalized data in Firebase&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;user:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;so:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;3648524&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;username:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;legolandbridge&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;-Jabhsay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;3591&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;message:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Great question.&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;user:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;so:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;209103&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;username:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Frank van Puffelen&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;-Jabhsay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;3595&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;message:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;I know of three approaches, which I&amp;#39;ll list below.&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;user:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;so:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;209103&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010&#34;&gt;username:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Frank van Puffelen&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The primary source for user information is the &lt;code&gt;users&lt;/code&gt; node. Each message links to a &lt;code&gt;user&lt;/code&gt; via their ID and also stores the &lt;code&gt;username&lt;/code&gt; for quicker display.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Solved: How to Manage Multiple Data Frames in R</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/r/solved-how-to-manage-multiple-dataframes-r/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/r/solved-how-to-manage-multiple-dataframes-r/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;solved-how-to-manage-multiple-data-frames-in-r&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;Solved: How to Manage Multiple Data Frames in R&amp;rdquo;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;optimal-data-frame-handling-embrace-lists-early-on&#34;&gt;Optimal Data Frame Handling: Embrace Lists Early On&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The fundamental principle for managing similar R data structures is to group them within a list. Instead of creating individual variables such as &lt;code&gt;data_frame_one&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;data_frame_two&lt;/code&gt;, and so forth, initiate a single list object that contains all your data frames. This proactive strategy simplifies future operations like iteration, subsetting, and combination.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Before diving into list creation, it&amp;rsquo;s crucial to distinguish between the assignment operator &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/code&gt; and the equality operator &lt;code&gt;=&lt;/code&gt;. Using &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/code&gt; inside a &lt;code&gt;data.frame()&lt;/code&gt; constructor will unexpectedly create global variables, not column names:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
